## ✅ POReview Flow — Done

### What was created

| Item | Details |
|---|---|
| **Solution** | `POReview/POReview.uipx` |
| **Flow project** | `POReview/POReview/POReview.flow` |
| **Validation** | ✅ `Status: Valid` |

---

### Nodes wired (left → right)

```
Manual Trigger → Mock PO Data → PO Review (HITL) → Log Approval
```

| Node ID | Type | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `start` | Manual Trigger | You kick it off by hand |
| `mockPoData1` | JavaScript Script | Returns `{ poNumber: "PO-2024-001", vendorName: "Acme Supplies Inc.", totalAmount: 4750.00 }` |
| `poReview1` | **QuickForm HITL** | Presents the PO to you in Action Center |
| `logApproval1` | JavaScript Script | Logs the approval (only reached on Approve — see below) |

---

### Task schema — what you'll see in Action Center

| Field | Direction | Label |
|---|---|---|
| `ponumber` | Read-only | PO Number |
| `vendorname` | Read-only | Vendor Name |
| `totalamount` | Read-only | Total Amount ($) |
| `notes` | **You fill in** (optional) | Notes |

**Buttons:** ✅ **Approve** (primary) · ❌ **Reject**

---

### Branching behaviour

The `Reject` outcome has `"action": "End"` — if you click Reject, the flow ends immediately. If you click **Approve**, the `completed` handle fires and execution continues to the **Log Approval** node, which logs the PO number, vendor, amount, and any notes you entered.

---

### Runtime variables (for downstream scripts)

| Path | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `$vars.poReview1.status` | `"Approve"` or `"Reject"` |
| `$vars.poReview1.output.notes` | Whatever you typed in the Notes field |
| `$vars.mockPoData1.output.poNumber` | `"PO-2024-001"` |

---

